-- title:
--   Hecke stability of the extendable m-torsion subgroup
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ lies in the set of nonunits of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`, consisting of a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over $\mathrm{base}\,p$ with a relative group law, and bijections identifying $JZero\,N_0$ and its reduction with the sections of $X$ over the generic and residue points; assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian`. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`: a smooth, separated, surjective group scheme $g \colon G \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ with connected fibres, a bijection $\mathrm{pts}$ from $JZero(N_0p)$ onto the sections of $g$ over the generic point which is additive, Galois-equivariant and Hecke-equivariant (each $t$ acting through an endomorphism $\varphi$ of $G$ over the base, `O.hecke`), together with the remaining fields of that structure. Let $m$ be a natural number, $m > 0$. Then, for the module structure `heckeModuleBar (N₀ * p)` of $\mathrm{HeckeAlg} = \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\mathrm{Nat.Primes}\,\mathbb{Z}$ on $JZero(N_0p)$ (evaluation at the Hecke operators when these commute, and the zero evaluation otherwise), the subgroup $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ — the subgroup generated by those $x$ which are $m$-torsion and satisfy `ExtendsToPlace A Λ.σA (O.pts x)`, recording that the corresponding point of $G$ extends over $A$ — is stable under the action of every $t \in \mathrm{HeckeAlg}$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-stability of the "finite part" of the $m$-torsion of the at-$p$ Néron object of $J_0(N_0p)$: the subgroup of $m$-torsion points whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points extend to $A$-points of the model. It is used when assembling the at-$p$ Néron data attached to a newform, and hence in the computations of the monodromy span and of the Frobenius–$U_p$ relation on the eigenplane in the Tate module of $JZero$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_smul_mem_finPts.lean

